{
 "case": "N10-PROVIDER-POS",
 "says": "Ana founds a Team and configures a Google connection for it that expects the hosted-domain claim example.com. On his own device Ben begins a sign-in for admission through that connection and completes it; the owner verifies the callback against the attempt's state and nonce and returns sign-in evidence carrying the hd claim, and nothing else. Ana first asks to admit Ben on that evidence while the Team's policy has no admission rule: the owner refuses it with claim_not_admitted. Ana then sets policy version 2, whose admission rule names that connection, the hosted_domain claim and the value example.com, bounded to read and use. The same claim, submitted again as a membership change naming the connection and policy version 2, commits Ben's provider-claim membership. What must come back is a membership whose standing names the connection and the policy that admitted it; what must not happen is an admission before a rule of the Team's own policy names that connection and claim.",
